1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,560
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:05,180
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:06,420
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:09,090
I've been an ironworker
for twenty-nine years.

5
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:10,750
Walking steel beams and
carrying

6
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,060
heavy loads all day.

7
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:12,910
I had my right knee

8
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:14,520
replaced two years ago.

9
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,930
It has hurt every day
since.

10
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:18,440
Not surgery pain.

11
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:19,560
I know what that felt
like,

12
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,230
and it went away.

13
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:21,340
This is different.

14
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:21,950
Tight.

15
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:22,910
Full.

16
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:23,670
Like a band around

17
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:25,360
the joint that never
loosens.

18
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:26,120
And for two years

19
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,590
I've been told the same
thing.

20
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:28,810
Give it time.

21
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:30,690
At six weeks it was
swelling,

22
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:32,160
and swelling is normal.

23
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,950
At three months,

24
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:34,330
give it six.

25
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:35,360
At six months,

26
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,800
some knees take a full
year.

27
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,550
At a year,

28
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:39,440
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

29
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,620
And I didn't just wait.

30
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,970
We went down the list.

31
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:43,340
More physical therapy.

32
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,410
Every session,

33
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:45,970
every exercise at home.

34
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:47,070
I got stronger.

35
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:48,700
The tightness never moved.

36
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,210
The pain pills helped,

37
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:51,520
and that was the problem.

38
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,210
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:54,120
and nobody could tell me

40
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:55,430
when I'd get to stop.

41
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,100
Then a nerve block.

42
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,030
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

43
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,330
And after that, a second

44
00:01:00,330 --> 00:01:01,430
operation to go back

45
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:02,960
in and do it over.

46
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,110
I said no.

47
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:05,760
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

48
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,760
and my knee felt like

49
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,590
a band was wrapped around
it,

50
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:11,100
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

51
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,780
Every morning I took
something

52
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,860
for it and went to work.

53
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:15,940
Couldn't do the stairs,

54
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:16,990
couldn't stand at the
counter

55
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:18,560
long enough to finish
dinner,

56
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:20,090
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

57
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:22,430
game without shifting
every two minutes.

58
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:23,710
Up on the iron,

59
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:25,040
the guys on my crew
started

60
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,890
carrying my share of the
load.

61
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:28,400
Nobody said anything.

62
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,680
It woke me at night,

63
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,710
and it turned ordinary
things,

64
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:33,050
like getting in the truck

65
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:34,410
or up off the couch,

66
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:35,640
into a decision.

67
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:36,800
After a long and serious

68
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,050
talk with my wife,

69
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:40,540
I went back in one more
time.

70
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,770
That was the fourth set

71
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:43,780
of X-rays on this knee.

72
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,370
And like the three before
it,

73
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:47,360
the answer was everything
looks great.

74
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,610
No loosening, no
infection,

75
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:50,860
nothing wrong.

76
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,370
Only this time there

77
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:54,180
was no new number.

78
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:55,150
Nobody said

79
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:56,350
give it another six
months.

80
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:58,320
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,080
I sat in the parking

82
00:01:59,080 --> 00:01:59,890
lot for a while.

83
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:01,080
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,490
Then explain this.

85
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:04,550
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:06,300
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,480
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:10,300
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,880
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,060
with my leg up,

91
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,730
trying to find any angle
where

92
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:16,050
it didn't feel like
something

93
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:17,730
was wrapped around my
knee

94
00:02:17,730 --> 00:02:18,860
and tightening.

95
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:19,520
I had to be on

96
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,990
the iron at seven.

97
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:23,510
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

98
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:25,430
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

99
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,370
And I just thought,

100
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:28,500
is this really my life
now?

101
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,190
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,780
Twenty-nine years on the
iron,

103
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,020
and my knee was going

104
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,300
to be what ended it?

105
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:36,350
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:37,170
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:38,710
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:38,710 --> 00:02:40,090
And when I found one,

109
00:02:40,090 --> 00:02:41,310
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:43,050
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:44,050
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:45,180
out and went looking.

113
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:46,400
Not for a product.

114
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,790
For an explanation.

115
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,530
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:51,860
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,750
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:55,520
And that's when I found

119
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,010
a video from a physical
therapist

120
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:57,600
named Dr.

121
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:00,020
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

122
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:01,930
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:03,970
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,390
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:07,580
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:08,650
The ice.

127
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:10,380
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,170
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:13,530
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:15,890
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:17,460
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,090
It's a preview.

133
00:03:19,090 --> 00:03:20,280
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,660
you this works fast.

135
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:22,740
It doesn't.

136
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,480
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,240
and to look at what's

138
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,600
going on around your new
knee

139
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,450
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:30,750
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:33,000
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,190
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:35,430
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:36,510
everything for me.

145
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:38,480
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,800
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,880
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,640
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,460
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,330
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:49,150
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,440
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,790
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:52,570
He said,

155
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,950
think about a swollen foot

156
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:55,510
inside a shoe.

157
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:56,970
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:59,370
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:03:59,370 --> 00:04:01,030
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:03,310
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,230
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:04,230 --> 00:04:05,880
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,450
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:10,420
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:12,460
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:15,830
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:17,210
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:18,800
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,680
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,480
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,560
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,950
So when you bend,

173
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:28,930
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:28,930 --> 00:04:30,010
When you straighten,

175
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:31,370
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:32,570
That's the band.

177
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:35,250
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,010
And you start being

179
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,070
the one who says,

180
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:38,150
you go ahead.

181
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:39,340
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,980
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:43,590
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:43,590 --> 00:04:45,720
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,840
around the knee.

186
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,550
Worth doing,

187
00:04:47,550 --> 00:04:48,540
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,000
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,230
taking up room.

190
00:04:51,230 --> 00:04:52,560
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,620
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,280
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,930
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:04:58,930 --> 00:05:00,450
finally calms down,

195
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:01,900
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,770
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,140
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,410
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,620
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,080
After two years of this,

201
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,970
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:12,970 --> 00:05:14,960
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:17,180
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,740
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:21,390
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:24,180
I'd bought knee pads,
knee sleeves,

207
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:26,530
compression braces,
creams,

208
00:05:26,530 --> 00:05:28,150
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:28,150 --> 00:05:29,580
and all any of it gave me

210
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,790
was an hour.

211
00:05:30,790 --> 00:05:31,780
I even looked at going

212
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,220
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:36,330
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:38,610
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:38,610 --> 00:05:40,170
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:41,550
Then one night I went

217
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:42,890
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:42,890 --> 00:05:45,010
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:45,010 --> 00:05:46,340
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,060
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:50,330
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:50,330 --> 00:05:51,780
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:53,650
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,810
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:57,410
This one device,

226
00:05:57,410 --> 00:05:59,000
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,590
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:02,960
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,770
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:06,290
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:08,310
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:08,310 --> 00:06:10,130
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:10,130 --> 00:06:12,610
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:12,610 --> 00:06:13,790
that if I ever found

235
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:14,990
something that helped,

236
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:16,080
I'd say so.

237
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,940
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,700
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,970
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:21,970 --> 00:06:23,010
It looked like the cheap

241
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:24,570
knee sleeves off Amazon

242
00:06:24,570 --> 00:06:26,220
that did nothing for me.

243
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,350
But I went to their
website anyway,

244
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:29,290
just to see what all

245
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:30,690
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:30,690 --> 00:06:32,340
It's the same red light
therapy

247
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:34,900
clinics charge $200 a
session

248
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,950
for, off machines that
cost

249
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,750
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:39,780
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:41,440
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,170
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:45,150
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:47,550
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:49,650
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:50,870
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:53,020
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,540
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,810
Ninety days.

260
00:06:55,810 --> 00:06:57,820
Results or your money
back,

261
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,570
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:02,290
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:05,140
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:07,160
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,500
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,780
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:11,230
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:11,230 --> 00:07:13,360
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,320
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,110
and I'd done it on

271
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:17,810
the steel for two years.

272
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:20,400
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:21,180
When it came,

274
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:23,710
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:25,130
because I'd been let down
too

276
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:27,060
many times to get excited.

277
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:28,490
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,330
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:31,850
More like it was coming
from inside

280
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:33,760
the knee and spreading
around it.

281
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:34,950
And that was it.

